From c839bbbc51c54d8f91a835f1bdfb68223721aa83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garrett Beasley <garrettbeasley@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:38:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] plugins/gpu: add a backend for Adreno GPUs driven by msm

The Linux backend only looks for display devices on the PCI bus, so a
Qualcomm SoC shows no GPU at all. Add the platform devices bound to the
adreno driver.

The frequency is read from the devfreq device and the temperature from
the thermal zones whose type starts with "gpu". The driver has no
system-wide load figure, so the usage is the engine time the DRM clients
report in fdinfo, summed per client id and divided by the time between
two updates. Only the clients of the current user are visible to the
daemon. /proc is searched for clients every five seconds, and only
while the usage sensor has a subscriber.

Video memory is left without a value: the GPU uses system memory and
buffers shared between clients cannot be told apart from fdinfo.
---
 plugins/gpu/CMakeLists.txt   |   2 +-
 plugins/gpu/LinuxBackend.cpp |  25 ++++
 plugins/gpu/LinuxMsmGpu.cpp  | 256 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 plugins/gpu/LinuxMsmGpu.h    |  60 ++++++++
 4 files changed, 342 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 plugins/gpu/LinuxMsmGpu.cpp
 create mode 100644 plugins/gpu/LinuxMsmGpu.h

